WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:04.204
-Hey, hey. All right. Thanks.
Sorry. A little sluggish.

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:05.504
Really did it up last night.

00:00:05.504 --> 00:00:07.606
I got to take it easy on
the booze, you know.

00:00:07.606 --> 00:00:08.741
My cousin's a doctor.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.476
He thinks we should
get rid of alcohol.

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:13.613
Said it kills 2 1/2 million
people every year, which is sad,

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:18.351
but, I mean, think of how many
people it produces.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:22.155
Yeah. It's got to be like
3-to-1, you know?

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.090
If my parents didn't drink,
I might not be here.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.025
I'm definitely going to
name my kids

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.127
after the substance
that got them conceived.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.696
"This is my daughter Tequila.
This is my son Jager."

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:32.031
"What about the kid
hugging your leg?"

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:38.038
"Ha! That's Molly."

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:40.940
Yeah, went out with my friend.
He's gay.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.742
We get along really well.
He's gay, I'm broke.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.843
I feel like poor people
and gay people

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.045
have a lot in common,
you know, right?

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:49.515
Both born that way.
Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:51.150
Women just want to be
our friends.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.187
And when you finally tell your
parents they're like,

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:57.223
"Yeah, we knew."

00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:04.296
Yeah. Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:04.296 --> 00:01:06.799
Yeah, we were drinking that
White Claw.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.668
You guys ever touched --
Yeah, that stuff's --

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:09.736
It's too much.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.036
I like White Claw
because it sounds like

00:01:11.036 --> 00:01:12.204
the new Marvel hero --

00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:13.839
White Claw, you know?

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:17.510
Sounds like Wolverine's
overprivileged nephew, you know?

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.278
White Claw's superpower
would be showing up

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:22.281
to a wedding in flip-flops
and driving his dad's boat

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:25.050
while hitting a Juul.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.853
Yeah. I'm doing better, though.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.754
I used to black out
four or five nights a week.

00:01:28.754 --> 00:01:29.855
I've cut back.

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:31.624
Now my phone
is my main addiction.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.658
Everybody goes,
"Hey, phone addiction --

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:33.726
better than alcohol."

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.494
I don't know. Same side effects.

00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:37.930
Both dangerous while driving,
both what I go to

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.999
when I'm nervous at a party,
and both have helped us

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:43.903
all sleep with
very regrettable people.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:46.106
Right? The phone is just
the new booze.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.607
Both are fun, but if you
do it too long,

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.075
it just becomes depressing.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.477
You know, you drink too much,
you're like, "I hate myself."

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:52.812
You look at your
phone too long you're like,

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.580
"Ah, even Jeff found love?

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:57.116
God!"
Yeah.

00:01:57.116 --> 00:02:02.054
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:04.657
It's too much. Too much. Yeah.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.125
My biggest fear used to be
the bar closing.

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:07.326
That was, like, my biggest fear.

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:09.628
Now my biggest fear is
my phone dying, you know?

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:10.697
Which is pretty good.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.198
100 years ago,
we had real problems.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.499
"My baby's got the black lung.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:14.933
She might not
make it through the night."

00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:16.135
I'm like, "I'm at 2%.

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.438
I might actually
have to feel something."

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:22.442
Yeah. I'm hooked. Oh, geez.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.844
Yeah, I actually carry
a battery pack on me

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.045
now in case my phone dies.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.413
That's insane.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:31.217
That's like carrying a flask to
fill up your empty flask.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.685
That's where I'm at.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.253
And I don't even know --
can you quit a phone?

00:02:34.253 --> 00:02:35.888
You know, like, If somebody
goes, "Hey, I gave up drinking,"

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:37.022
I go, "Good for you."

00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:38.257
If somebody goes,
"Hey, I gave up my phone,"

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:40.727
I'm like,
"How did you get here?"

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.362
Yeah. The phone is
ruining our lives.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.529
It's bad.

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:44.964
You know, I was walking down
Third Avenue.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:47.500
I was next to a homeless guy.
He was drunk. I was on my phone.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.401
We were doing the same stuff,
you know?

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:50.569
He's yelling about
the government.

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:52.171
I'm tweeting at Trump,
you know?

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.106
He's creepily staring
at beautiful women.

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:56.209
I'm scrolling through Instagram,
you know?

00:02:56.209 --> 00:03:00.112
He's flashing everybody.
I'm sending a photo of mine.

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:05.051
Yeah. I don't know.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.687
Yeah, we don't know how
to connect anymore.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.655
You know, my friend just got
dumped, so I took him out,

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:11.657
tried to wing-man him,
meet some ladies for him.

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:14.026
Didn't go too well.
You know, he got upset.

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:16.462
He's like, "Screw this.
Let's go to a strip club."

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:17.563
I don't get that logic.

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:19.298
You know, to me,
that's like going fishing,

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:21.433
not catching anything,
and being like, "Screw this.

00:03:21.433 --> 00:03:24.837
Let's go to the aquarium."

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:28.474
It's the same thing.
Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.710
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, yeah.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.879
The only difference is --
no one leaves an aquarium going,

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:37.550
"I tell you -- I think that
flounder was into me.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:41.754
That's one hot piece of bass."
Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:44.390
I don't know.
We'll figure it out.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.492
I got to figure something out.
I'm 35.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:47.793
You know, I'm at the age
where all my friends

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:49.228
are getting divorced.

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:51.864
And, yeah, it's tough.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.533
I'm surprised people still
want to get married.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.234
That shocks me,
especially younger people.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:58.304
They're so against traditional
stuff, you know?

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.539
But, yet, every lady I know
is dying to get married,

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:01.708
which blows my mind.

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.509
Ladies, you've come so far,
so much progress,

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.877
but, yet, when it comes
to marriage,

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.478
you guys get very old-fashioned.

00:04:06.478 --> 00:04:09.014
"I want the ring and the dress
and the party."

00:04:09.014 --> 00:04:12.251
What? Grow up.

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:14.687
Ladies, you're killing it.
Go frolic, be free.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.388
"But it's my special day."

00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:19.358
All right.
Why do you have to ruin mine?

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:20.426
I don't know.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.861
But that's why you ladies
are brilliant.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.763
You gals are geniuses, ladies,
because you guys tend to be

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.064
the ones who want to get
married, yet, somehow,

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:27.600
you've designed it
to where the man asks you.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.237
That's some Jedi-level
mind trickery right there.

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:34.607
Yes. Well-played. Right?

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:38.043
Genius, ladies. Genius.
You're like Yoda.

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:39.545
"I want to get married,
but you'll ask me."

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.046
Yes. You got it.

00:04:41.046 --> 00:04:42.248
"And you'll get down
on one knee."

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.349
No problem.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:45.217
"And you'll buy me
an expensive ring."

00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:46.419
Will do.

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:49.488
"And whose idea was this?"
All Mine.

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:50.756
Well-played, ladies.
Well-played.

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:51.890
I don't know.
Am I nuts?

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.058
Marriage just feels like
the least-romantic thing

00:04:53.058 --> 00:04:54.093
on the planet.

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:55.661
It's legal. Ugh!

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:56.829
Got to go to a courthouse,
get a license.

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.163
What's the license for?

00:04:58.163 --> 00:05:00.065
That's the only license
we don't check, by the way.

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:01.834
Driver's license,
liquor license.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:02.868
People check a fishing license.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:05.304
I'm gonna start checking
marriage license.

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:07.239
Next time I see a
short, broke, weird guy --

00:05:07.239 --> 00:05:08.640
he's like, "That's my hot wife
over there" --

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.777
I'm gonna be like,
"Let me see some I.D."

00:05:11.777 --> 00:05:13.946
Thanks a lot. I'm Kevin Hart.
Thank you.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.115
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.751
-Hey!

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:22.522
Mark Normand.

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:26.559
For more info, visit
marknormandcomedy.com.

